// doors-and-locks.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for doors, locks, and keys (docs/01 chapters 3 and 5). The
// `door` kind is `openable` and `fixed` by default; add `lockable`, `locked`,
// and `unseal_with <key>` to make it lock. A door joins two rooms with
// `in A, B`, the EXISTENCE form: one door, fully present in both rooms,
// listed on both sides, one state. A room's exit points at the DOOR rather
// than a room, so crossing it is gated on the door being open and unlocked
// and lands you on the far side, with no author code at all. Compile and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/doors-and-locks.storyarc -o doors.z5
//   frotz doors.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   east                      barred: the door is locked, so you do not move
//   open door                 refused: you cannot open a locked door
//   unlock door               no key named: the library reaches for the door's
//                             own key and says so, "(with the brass key)",
//                             then the door's own unlock line (its alter)
//   lock door                 the same reach, the other way
//   open door with key        one line: the REAL unlock runs first (the
//                             door's own unlock line again), then the open
//   east                      the way is clear; you step through to the vault
//   west                      and back again, through the same door
//   close door / lock door with key / unlock door with key
//                             a named key needs no telling: no parenthetical
//
// The door is a single object shared by both rooms (`in hall, vault`), reachable
// and operable from either side, and Cosmos handles the lock logic, the open
// gate, and the step to the far side. There is no `on go` handler anywhere here.

game
    title  "The Locked Vault"
    headline "A doors-and-locks showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  hall

room hall
    name "The Entrance Hall"
    desc "A bare stone hall. A heavy oak door is set into the east wall."
    east oak_door

room vault
    name "The Vault"
    desc "A close, windowless vault. A door leads back west to the hall."
    west oak_door

// One door object, present in both rooms. It is openable and fixed by virtue of
// the door kind; the lock and its key are declared here.
thing oak_door of door in hall, vault
    name "oak door"
    words >oak, door
    lockable
    locked
    unseal_with brass_key

    // The door's own report for UNLOCK, in its own words, the default
    // mechanics kept (alter, docs/01 chapter 11). It answers for OPEN DOOR
    // WITH KEY too, since that runs the real unlock first. `second` is
    // what the player typed: nothing on a bare UNLOCK, when the library
    // has already said which key it used.
    on unlock
        alter block
            if second is nothing
                say "The old lock turns over with a heavy clunk."
            else
                say "You turn ${the second}, and the old lock gives."
        continue

thing brass_key in player
    name "brass key"
    words >brass, key
